{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1127555-how-do-area-spells-work-in-mage-20th","id":1127555,"title":"How do area spells work in Mage 20th?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T04:04:17-07:00","id":1127555,"title":"How do area spells work in Mage 20th?","content":"Moin,<br /> <br /> are there any rules to cast area spells in Mage 20th? I just wonder how to create spells, that for example<ul><li>feed of peoples energy or enrapture people during a concert</li> <li>create a circle of protection</li> <li>make a bunch of people forget recent events (Men in Black Style)</li> <li>create a fireball (Yeah, vulgar as hell) etc.</li> </ul>I am not interested in the combination of spheres to actually make these effects because in my humble opinion this is the most fun part in Mage.<br /> I'd rather like to know how to add the area component to all imaginable spells. <br /> <br /> So far I didn't find anything (Mage 20th, M20 How do you DO that, M20 Book of Secrets), only hints. For example: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">At this Rank, the scale of effect grows larger, now</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">encompassing several dozen yards or a handful of characters. (Mage 20th, Forces 3, page 516)</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Of course one could use the &quot;Optional Dividing Successes Rule&quot; (Mage 20th, page 504) to </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">target each and every person within a radius but it doesn't sound right. A mage would need to cast rituals with hundreds of successes (rock star mage, 1. example).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I could of course use the rules of </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mage the Awakening</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, but I prefer the storyteller-system of the classic World of Darkness and I wish I could make it work for Mage 20th.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14340-epimenides","name":"epimenides","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:16:00-07:00","id":1127574,"title":"","content":"Area-Of-Effect rules have always been rather vague in mage. You won't find any hard rules like with most other effect properties.<br /> <br /> The standard rules either say '<i>As many people as you have successes</i>' or '<i>one extra target per extra success</i>' if you use the split-successes rule.<br /> And then we get into things like Forces 4/5 which can cause big area damage, wards that grow X feet per success in radius, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, go with what seems appropriate for the magic in question. For example, I'd argue that an effect that uses sound to affect the mind is *perfect* for affecting a lot of people, without rolling hundreds of successes. The disadvantage is that it will affect friend or foe. Heh.<br /> Likewise the Technocracy's NWO definitely uses media to mass-effect people and wipe memories.<br /> <br /> The best rule remains: 'ST Call and what Feels Right'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:59:59-07:00","id":1127584,"title":"","content":"There is that procedure in Guide to the Technocracy that allows you to Target a crowd. You roll to see what level of will power your speech overcomes. Then anyone who is below that, and part of the crowd is convinced you're telling the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:03:57-07:00","id":1127610,"title":"","content":"It all comes down to the specifics of the effect you're attempting, and the instruments you're using to accomplish it. The rules for targeting individuals is for when you're targeting a specific pattern and don't really apply if you're creating a blast of fire or shockwave of concussive sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:09:12-07:00","id":1127611,"title":"","content":"In M20 there's a few vague guidelines, if my memory doesn't fail. &quot;Successes table&quot; has fluff about affecting lots of people or an area, you need at least 5 successes to affect an area, and affecting a largue croud would be arround 15-20 successes. Also, Forces has examples of the areas of effect you can target at each Sphere Level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:52:39-07:00","id":1128847,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the advice! I just don't understand how these rules could gone missing since Mage 20th really got an overhaul compared to previous editions and area spells are well implemented in Mage the Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14340-epimenides","name":"epimenides","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:01:02-07:00","id":1128850,"title":"","content":"Of course a clever player can break whatever rule you come up with through use of mid level correspondence by using what's similar about the targets to make them count as one target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:54:35-07:00","id":1128874,"title":"","content":"True! Very nice idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14340-epimenides","name":"epimenides","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}